                        "question": "<p>A tension rigging cable pulls with a force magnitude $F = 500\\text{ N}$ oriented at an angle $\\theta = 36.87^\\circ$ above the positive horizontal $x$-axis (where $\\cos 36.87^\\circ = 0.80$ and $\\sin 36.87^\\circ = 0.60$).</p>\n<p>The rectangular Cartesian components ($F_x, F_y$) of the tension force are:</p>\n<div class=\"grid grid-cols-2 gap-2 my-2 font-mono text-xs\">\n  <div class=\"p-2 bg-slate-900/80 rounded border border-slate-700/60\">(A) $F_x = 300 N,\\quad F_y = 400 N$</div>\n  <div class=\"p-2 bg-slate-900/80 rounded border border-slate-700/60\">(B) $F_x = 400 N,\\quad F_y = 300 N$</div>\n  <div class=\"p-2 bg-slate-900/80 rounded border border-slate-700/60\">(C) $F_x = 250 N,\\quad F_y = 433 N$</div>\n  <div class=\"p-2 bg-slate-900/80 rounded border border-slate-700/60\">(D) $F_x = 354 N,\\quad F_y = 354 N$</div>\n</div>",
