                        "solution": "<p><strong class=\"text-emerald-400\">Step 1: Identify the Error Condition</strong></p>\n<p>Rejecting $H_0$ when $H_0$ is true is by definition a <strong>Type I error</strong> (false positive).</p>\n<p><strong class=\"text-emerald-400\">Step 2: Determine Probability</strong></p>\n<p>The probability of making a Type I error is exactly the significance level $\\alpha = 0.05$.</p>\n<p class=\"mt-2 pt-2 border-t border-emerald-500/20\"><strong class=\"text-cyan-300\">Correct Answer:</strong> <span class=\"text-emerald-300 font-bold\">(A) Type I error with probability $\\alpha = 0.05$</span></p>\n<p class=\"text-[11px] text-slate-400\"><em>FE Exam Tip:</em> $\\alpha = P(\\text{Reject } H_0 \\mid H_0 \\text{ true}) = \\text{Type I error}$. $\\beta = P(\\text{Accept } H_0 \\mid H_0 \\text{ false}) = \\text{Type II error}$.</p>"
